Subject: [PATCH] slimbus: qcom-ngd: wait up to 5 s for the QMI service

The second half of omarchy-mobile f702f68
devices/oneplus7pro/kernel/audio/slim-ngd-pd-up-race.patch (the ordering half
is 0033). rc4 boots on guacamole log "QMI wait timeout" ~1 s after the NGD
controller registers, and the same boots return all-zero microphone capture
with the full WCD934x DAPM path powered and the TX0 port never underflowing.
This is a test of whether the 1 s wait is too short; it is not yet a proven fix.
Nura-Category: local-workaround
Nura-Origin: omarchy-mobile f702f688 slim-ngd-pd-up-race (2/2)
Upstream-Status: not in mainline v7.2 (timeout still 1 s)
---
--- a/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c	2026-11-13 19:47:39.467036689 +0100
+++ b/drivers/slimbus/qcom-ngd-ctrl.c	2026-11-13 19:47:39.467462025 +0100
@@ -1455,7 +1455,7 @@
 
 	/* Make sure qmi service is up before continuing */
 	if (!wait_for_completion_interruptible_timeout(&ctrl->qmi_up,
-						       msecs_to_jiffies(MSEC_PER_SEC))) {
+						       msecs_to_jiffies(5 * MSEC_PER_SEC))) {
 		dev_err(ctrl->dev, "QMI wait timeout\n");
 		return;
 	}
